@startuml ai-sdlc-adapter
title ai-sdlc — platform adapter dispatch (scripts/platform/contract.md)
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam wrapWidth 280

start
:caller (skill, command, agent, CI template,
docs/agents/issue-tracker.md) runs
sdlc-platform [--platform github|azure] [--dry-run] [--mock] <function> [args];
note right
  Callers never run gh, az or glab directly.
  12 functions: platform_detect, work_item_create,
  work_item_get, work_item_link, work_item_comment,
  pr_create, pr_get, pr_comment, pr_checks,
  branch_protect_apply, ci_workflow_install, metrics_export
end note

:resolve platform in order;
if (--platform given?) then (yes)
  :use it;
elseif ($SDLC_PLATFORM set?) then (yes)
  :use it;
elseif (platform in sdlc.config.json\n(both / auto defer)?) then (concrete)
  :use it;
else (defer / absent)
  :scripts/platform/_detect.sh on the "origin" remote;
endif

if (platform == none?) then (yes)
  :exit 3 for everything except platform_detect;
  stop
else (no)
endif

if (--mock or SDLC_PLATFORM_MOCK=1?) then (yes)
  :prepend scripts/platform/_mocks/bin to PATH
  fake gh/az: counters + created items in $SDLC_MOCK_STATE,
  every invocation appended to $SDLC_MOCK_LOG;
else (no)
endif
if (--dry-run or SDLC_DRY_RUN=1?) then (yes)
  :run against mocks with a temporary log,
  print each CLI command as "+ <cmd>", no JSON result;
  stop
else (no)
endif

:exec scripts/platform/<platform>/<function>.sh
sources _root.sh then _common.sh (=> _lib.sh, _project.sh)
helpers: out_json, md_to_html, require_gh, require_az,
az_context, not_supported;

:print exactly one JSON object on one line
identical field names and types on both platforms
unsupplied field = null (never omitted), ids are strings,
bodies always passed as files, no silent no-ops;

if (outcome) then (0)
  :success;<<#C8E6C9>>
elseif (1) then
  :failed — stderr starts with "ai-sdlc:";<<#FFCDD2>>
elseif (2) then
  :usage;<<#FFE0B2>>
elseif (3) then
  :not supported on this platform (exact message form);<<#FFE0B2>>
else (8)
  :pending — pr_checks only;<<#FFF9C4>>
endif

:scripts/platform/conformance.sh [--platform github|azure|all]
scratch repo per platform, every function under mocks,
jq assertions on exit codes + stdout shapes,
idempotency of work_item_link and branch_protect_apply,
exact not-supported message, static check that no Azure script
mentions gh and no GitHub script mentions az,
then diffs normalised key sets between platforms — exit 1 on first divergence;
stop
@enduml
